    "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented the `--threshold` feature for `frai eval`. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n### Core Changes (frai-core)\n\n**`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`**\n- Modified `generateReport()` to accept an optional `thresholds` parameter\n- Added threshold evaluation logic that checks each metric's score against specified minimums\n- Returns `passed` boolean (true if all thresholds pass or no thresholds specified)\n- Returns `thresholds` array with one entry per threshold containing: metric, min, score, and passed status\n\n**`packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`**\n- Updated Markdown reporter to include a \"Thresholds\" section showing PASS/FAIL status for each threshold\n- JSON reporter automatically includes the new fields via JSON.stringify\n\n### CLI Changes (frai-cli)\n\n**`packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`**\n- Added `--threshold <metric=min>` option (repeatable)\n- Implemented `parseThresholds()` function that:\n  - Validates format (`metric=value`)\n  - Ensures values are between 0 and 1\n  - Verifies metric IDs are valid\n  - Returns appropriate error messages\n- Modified `runEvalCommand()` to:\n  - Parse threshold arguments\n  - Exit with code 2 for malformed/invalid thresholds\n  - Exit with code 1 if any threshold fails\n  - Exit with code 0 if all thresholds pass (or no thresholds specified)\n\n### Tests\n\nAdded 6 new comprehensive tests in `packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`:\n- \u2705 Thresholds pass when metric score meets minimum\n- \u2705 Thresholds fail when metric score is below minimum\n- \u2705 Thresholds fail when metric has no score (null)\n- \u2705 Report passes with no thresholds specified\n- \u2705 Markdown report includes threshold section\n- \u2705 JSON report includes passed and thresholds fields\n\nAll new tests **pass**. The two pre-existing test failures remain unchanged as noted.\n\n## Feature Behavior\n\n```bash\n# Passing threshold - exit 0\nfrai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9\n\n# Failing threshold - exit 1\nfrai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=0.95\n\n# Invalid threshold value - exit 2\nfrai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=1.5\n\n# Unknown metric - exit 2\nfrai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json --threshold unknown=0.9\n\n# Multiple thresholds\nfrai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json \\\n  --threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.8 --threshold length_variance=0.7\n```\n\nReports (JSON and Markdown) include threshold evaluation results even if command fails.",
